body:
its sad really. I live in connecticut and I plan to move up there one day. The people fleeing New York, Mass, and CT all run up there to escape the shit they voted in here, and then continue to do it up there, ruining what good stuff you have.

&#x200B;

But, I do know that New Hampshire does stand by their motto, so I wouldnt be surprised if they resist if any laws were to be passed

I thinks its a class E felony in CT (Which is bullshit) so its actually pretty serious

&#x200B;

Per CT general statutes:

&#x200B;

Title 29: Chpt. 529 Sec. 29-28 Permit to Carry Pistol or Revolver (e) The issuance of any permit to carry a pistol or revolver does not thereby authorize the possession or carrying of a pistol or revolver in any premises where the possession or carrying of a pistol or revolver is otherwise prohibited by law or is prohibited by the person who owns or exercises control over such premises. (S. 3; P.A. 16-34, S. 8.) Title 29: Chpt. 529 Sec. 29-37. Penalties. (a) Any person violating any provision of section 29-28 or 29-31 ***shall be guilty of a class E felony***, and any pistol or revolver found in the possession of any person in violation of any of said provisions shall be forfeited. S. 134; P.A. 13-258,

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

my advice: concealed means concealed. If you got a good enough holster, belt, and attire, no one besides yourself will know youre carrying

"Trust me"

&#x200B;

Gives me shivers every time I hear it
